KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cross-cast to the sibling subobject: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dereferenced function pointer must be.*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [expr.dynamic.cast]/9.2: dynamic_cast<iface_b *>(p) with p pointing
to the iface_a subobject of an impl object yields a pointer to its iface_b
subobject.  The front end models the run-time check as a nondeterministic
choice between null and the unadjusted, reinterpreted pointer.  The test
used to accept the value 1 that the call through that pointer could
produce (calling iface_a::a through iface_b's slot); since virtual calls
take their candidates from the virtual tables (remove_function_pointers),
that call fails "dereferenced function pointer must be impl::b..."
instead.  The cross-cast must adjust to the target subobject of the
most-derived object.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.
